# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: findboards
# board: discover
# Finding boards, from a shell that was never told to look.
#
# Opening every serial port on a machine is not a thing to do to a desk
# uninvited: the ports belong to whatever else is on them until a person
# says otherwise.  So the shell looks when it is ASKED -- and what it
# finds is offered wherever boards are useful, without the applications
# being told separately.
wait 60
note nothing is mounted: this desktop was not told to look
click 980 30
wait 10
expect-menu Settings|Find boards|Applications
menu-pick Find boards
wait 400
note what answered is mounted and named, in the shell's own menu
click 980 30
wait 10
expect-menu tiku
note and the editor offers to run on one, though nobody told IT anything;
note the menu is still open from the reading above, so it is picked from
menu-pick Programming
wait 10
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 250
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Run on tiku
quit
